{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"b3cab00338425c0da6d741f037644050ffaa3e47"},"timestamp":1578643574,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWU1NDc5MjcxOTM=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/4006","origin":"github"},"title":"publish disregards git configuration to push all branches","message":"(basically, this issue restates #1284)\n\nDesired behavior: I want to automatically ``publish`` all branches of a dataset with `datalad publish` to a remote, instead of only the master and git-annex branch.\n\nTo do this, I configured the remote in question in ``.git/config`` with ``git config --local remote.\u003cremote-name\u003e.push 'refs/heads/*' ``.\n\nA ``git push [\u003cremote-name\u003e]`` pushes all branches, as requested. ``datalad publish --to \u003csibling-name\u003e`` does not care about this configuration, and only pushes master and git-annex.\n\nThe culprit is in here: https://github.com/datalad/datalad/blob/a1554a95fbcd07254bc3faaa797133039f237272/datalad/distribution/publish.py#L462","files":null}]}